# Rank 1309 / CVE-2021-3311: October CMS's authentication manager cleared the
# logged-out user's session data but never rotated the session identifier
# itself, so a session ID an attacker had captured before logout came back to
# life the next time the same user logged in (CWE-613).
#
# Auth/Manager::logout() in src/Auth/Manager.php called Session::flush(),
# which empties the session's stored data but leaves the session ID (and its
# backing store record) intact. A subsequent login re-populated that same
# session under the same ID rather than issuing a new one, so a cookie
# captured while the victim was still logged in kept working across a
# logout/login cycle: good logs in, bad captures the cookie, good logs out
# (the captured cookie stops working), good logs in again, and the captured
# cookie is valid once more because it names the same session slot.
#
# Pool commit 642f597489e6 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK). It replaces
# Session::flush() with Session::invalidate(), which both clears the session
# data and regenerates the session ID, so a captured pre-logout identifier
# can never be revived by a later login. No pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap. Scanning either revision reports 0 findings.
# code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication is the nearest concept,
# already declined for the same reasoning at rank 1110 (NextAuth config) and
# rank 1115 (FOSSBilling password change): it carries CWE_384 rather than
# this CVE's CWE_613, and its reviewCondition, "authentication completes
# without rotating or invalidating the existing HTTP session", is written for
# the moment a session begins (login), not the moment one ends (logout). Its
# only binding is Java's `setAuthentication` + `getSession` idiom at login;
# nothing recognizes a logout handler at all, in any language. Stating the
# general condition — a logout handler clears session data without also
# rotating the identifier, so a stolen cookie can be revived by the victim's
# next login — needs recognizing "logout" as its own security-relevant event
# distinct from login, which is judgement rather than a port, and is exactly
# the category the same nearest concept was already kept narrow to avoid at
# rank 1115.
#
# No definition change attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1309: logout clears session data without rotating the session id"
  lang php
  file src/Auth/Manager.php
  reject_review code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication
  code
  ```
  class Manager
  {
      public function logout()
      {
          if (is_null($this->user) && !$this->check()) {
              return;
          }

          if ($this->user) {
              $this->user->setRememberToken(null);
              $this->user->forceSave();
          }

          $this->user = null;

          Session::flush();
          Cookie::queue(Cookie::forget($this->sessionKey));
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1309: logout invalidates the session, rotating the session id"
  lang php
  file src/Auth/Manager.php
  reject_review code.MissingSessionRotationAfterAuthentication
  code
  ```
  class Manager
  {
      public function logout()
      {
          if (is_null($this->user) && !$this->check()) {
              return;
          }

          if ($this->user) {
              $this->user->setRememberToken(null);
              $this->user->forceSave();
          }

          $this->user = null;

          Session::invalidate();
          Cookie::queue(Cookie::forget($this->sessionKey));
      }
  }
  ```
